{"content":"# Thread `PRRT_kwDOTXdlLc6sGjPV` — `float(v)` hardening (E5 completion)

Fixed in `bench/harbor_fa/summary.py` (`_trial_rows`), folding the rewards read into the same E5 tolerant pattern as `exception_info`/`agent_result`:

- a **non-dict** `verifier_result.rewards` (truthy garbage) degrades to no-rewards instead of `AttributeError` on `.values()`;
- **non-numeric reward values** are skipped (`try: float(v) except (TypeError, ValueError): pass` — the suggested shape), so `{"r": "high"}` / `{"r": null}` render as scored-and-unresolved instead of killing the whole summary; numeric values in a mixed dict still score.

